# Test: `bus { participant <path> }` compiles identically to a participant's own `bus` section, merges identical declarations naming both origins, and refuses disagreements at validate, reload, and start.
# QUESTION: when group `transit` (holding peers `t1` and `t2`) is limited four ways:
# (a) `bgp { group transit { bus { receive { from [ /bus/endpoint/collector ]; } } } }`,
# (b) `bus { participant /bgp/group/transit { receive { from [ /bus/endpoint/collector ]; } } }`,
# (c) both identical, and (d) both disagreeing (section names `/bus/endpoint/collector`,
# central names `/bgp/peer/edge1`): do (a), (b), and (c) validate and load via live reload
# with identical effective `receive` rules for `t1` and `t2` in `| implied | json` (except
# origin/source, with (c) naming both places), and is (d) refused at `ze config validate`,
# SIGHUP reload, and `ze start` naming both lines and saying to keep one?
# A unit test cannot decide this because it proves offline validation, live SIGHUP reload,
# daemon startup refusal, and `show config running | implied | json` parity end to end.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-explicit-plugin-and-attach-config S39 / AC-42.
# PREVENTS: central `bus > participant` blocks diverging from own-section `bus` blocks,
# silently overwriting disagreeing rules instead of refusing, or failing to attribute both
# origins when written identically in both places.

option=timeout:value=120s
option=env:var=ZE_CONFIG_DIR:value=.
option=env:var=XDG_DATA_HOME:value=.
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass

stdin=init-answers:terminator=EOF_INIT
admin
testpass
127.0.0.1
$PORT2
EOF_INIT

tmpfs=collector.sh:mode=755:terminator=EOF_COL
#!/bin/sh
while IFS= read -r _; do
	:
done
EOF_COL

# (a) Own section only.
tmpfs=cfg-a.conf:terminator=EOF_CFGA
system {
	authentication {
		# bcrypt cost-4 hash of "testpass".
